# Backend-scoped ignores for the FastAPI application.
#
# The repository-root .gitignore already covers everything here: its patterns
# are deliberately de-anchored so they match at any depth (see
# docs/repository-structure.md, "The 2026-09-09 restructure"). This file is the
# conventional per-app copy — keep the two consistent, and prefer the root file
# for anything that should apply to frontend/ as well.
#
# NOTE: data-generator/generated/**/*.csv and data-generator/discovery/* are
# TRACKED on purpose — they are the synthetic dataset and the live SAP
# discovery snapshot the frontend builds against. Nothing here may ignore them.

# --- Virtual environments ---
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Byte-compiled / cache ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so

# --- Packaging / build ---
build/
dist/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/

# --- Testing and type checking ---
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# --- Environment files ---
# Real env files are never committed; the template is. This also covers the
# CPI credentials in data-generator/.env — do not narrow it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
*.pem
*.log

# --- Archives ---
# An archive can carry files every rule above would have excluded -- a handover
# zip of this folder contains .env, credentials and all. Because git sees only
# the archive, no .env rule can help. So they are ignored by default; use -f
# deliberately if you ever need to track one.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.7z
*.rar

# --- Local dev convenience scripts ---
# Machine-specific launcher (Docker Desktop + backend + frontend). Never shared.
start-dev.bat
